       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (up to 2,000 mg/day for extended-release).\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg in one dose is well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. A dose that high raises the risk of serious GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1700 mg/day total:** for example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO** at a different frequency.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give a reason. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy before I enter it."
